---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
---
<Base title="Set up FieldADE" description="How to install FieldADE on your iPhone, pair it with HomeADE, and start a chat. Includes phone-only setup with no Mac.">
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + 2rem)">
    <div class="wrap guide">
      <h1>Set up FieldADE</h1>
      <p>FieldADE is the iPhone app. It shows what is due, your mail and texts, and a chat with the assistants on your Mac. Pair it with <a href="/homeade">HomeADE</a>, which has to be running on that Mac. If HomeADE is not installed yet, <a href="/homeade/setup">set up the Mac first</a>. Pairing takes a few minutes once the Mac shows a code.</p>
      <p><a href="/fieldade">About FieldADE</a></p>

      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>An iPhone with iOS 17 or later.</li>
        <li>HomeADE on a Mac, with a pairing code on the screen. Or skip the Mac and <a href="#no-mac">use the phone on its own</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="phone">1. Install FieldADE</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fieldade/id6828288883" rel="noopener">Install FieldADE from the App Store</a>.</li>
        <li>Open FieldADE.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="pair">2. Pair it with your Mac</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>On the Mac, HomeADE's window should show a pairing code. If it does not, click the antenna icon and choose <strong>Pair a phone…</strong>. The <a href="/homeade/setup">HomeADE setup</a> gets you to that window.</li>
        <li>In FieldADE, open <strong>Settings → Machines → Scan a pairing code</strong>.</li>
        <li>Point the camera at the code on your Mac.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The code holds your Mac's key, so do not share it or post a picture of it. If the phone cannot scan, click <strong>Copy the link instead</strong> on the Mac, send the link to the phone, and tap it. The link asks before it applies.</p>
      <p>The phone reaches the Mac through relay.embry.dev, so it works away from home with nothing else to install. The traffic is encrypted with a key that only your phone and your Mac hold. See the <a href="/fieldade/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="first-chat">3. Start a chat</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>On the phone, tap <strong>+</strong> and pick a folder for the chat.</li>
        <li>Type a question about your notes and send it.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Before the assistant edits a file or runs a command, the phone asks you to allow or deny it. The same chat is open in the HomeADE window when you sit down at the Mac.</p>

      <h2 id="more">Add more</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Calendars.</strong> On the phone, open <strong>Settings → Choose sources → Calendars</strong>. Sign in to Google, sign in to iCloud with an app-specific password, or allow access to the calendars on the phone.</li>
        <li><strong>Codex or Grok.</strong> Install the tool on the Mac and sign in. HomeADE lists it under <strong>Settings → Agents on this machine</strong>. <a href="/homeade/setup#more">HomeADE setup</a> has that step.</li>
        <li><strong>Share sheet.</strong> Share a photo, file, or link to FieldADE and it lands in your vault's Inbox. Items shared while the Mac is away wait on the phone.</li>
        <li><strong>Widget.</strong> On iOS 26 or later, add the FieldADE widget to the home screen.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="no-mac">Without a Mac</h2>
      <p>FieldADE can run on its own. Open <strong>Settings → Phone alone</strong>, turn on <strong>Phone only</strong>, pick a vault folder on the phone, and enter an Anthropic API key. Chats then run on the phone and bill that key. To look around first, tap <strong>Try the sample vault</strong> on the Today screen.</p>

      <h2 id="windows">Windows</h2>
      <p>The Windows build is HomeADE, and the beta cannot pair a phone yet. <a href="/homeade/setup#windows">Windows setup</a> covers the installer and the warning Windows shows.</p>

      <h2 id="trouble">If something goes wrong</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The phone says to set the Mac's address.</strong> The phone is not paired. Do step 2.</li>
        <li><strong>The phone says "no end-to-end key."</strong> Make a new pairing code on the Mac and scan it again.</li>
        <li><strong>Chats do not start.</strong> On the Mac, check that Claude Code is installed and signed in, then click <strong>Restart HomeADE…</strong> in the menu. <a href="/homeade/setup#trouble">HomeADE troubleshooting</a> covers a window that says it has no token.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Still stuck? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .guide { max-width: 44rem; }
  .guide h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; scroll-margin-top: 6.5rem; }
  .guide ol, .guide ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .guide li { margin: .35rem 0; }
</style>
